{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050", "score": 0.123, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-050 | Study family SF-APPA-050: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star\n- observed_research_question: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: A specific opponent play type on the preceding possession suppresses each star's next-possession PPP relative to that star's baseline.\n- observed_result: PUTBACK is top suppressor for 6+ stars (e.g. D. Mitchell 1.178 to 0.884, d=-0.294, n_after=95; B. Beal d=-0.345 n=32; C. Holmgren d=-0.222 n=52). Other tops: TRANSITION (A. Davis -0.058), POST_UP (N. Jokic -0.075), PULL_ [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: No multiplicity correction; n_after is 32-95 for several PUTBACK cells vs thousands of baseline possessions.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 30 stars; min n_after=30\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025", "score": 0.121, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-025 | Study family SF-CHT-025: Play-type labeling audit: OTHER/DRIVE foul leakage\n- observed_research_question: Play-type labeling audit: OTHER/DRIVE foul leakage\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: Play-type PPP differences are real efficiency, not labeling/foul artifacts.\n- observed_result: OTHER: 36% end in fouls, PPP inflated (FOUL_BUCKET). DRIVE: 12pp below foul benchmark (FOUL_LEAK). PNR shows 22% foul rate. Only 335 of 50,668 possessions (0.7%) map to a real play type via initiation_type.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- observed_failure_evidence: OTHER PPP inflated by 36% foul endings; DRIVE 12pp below foul benchmark; initiation_type maps 0.7%.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 50,668 possessions in the initiation_type check\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Per-PT diagnostic of foul-ending share vs PPP; initiation_type mapping.\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "score": 0.119, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-005 | Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- observed_research_question: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.\n- observed_result: Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 523 cells; 440 pairs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-074", "score": 0.112, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-074 | Study family SF-APPS-074: Gravity persistence: elite creator -> teammate PPP at lags 1-3\n- observed_research_question: Gravity persistence: elite creator -> teammate PPP at lags 1-3\n- auto_outcome_status: rejected\n- observed_hypothesis: After an elite creator's signature action, teammates score more on the team's next k possessions with the same lineup on the floor.\n- observed_result: All 8 creators horizon=0. Jokic lag-1 ATT=+0.0282 CI[-0.043,+0.099] p=0.3779. CLEAN NULL on teammate PPP. Secondary: Antetokounmpo +0.075 distinct initiators over next 3 poss (perm p=0.0002, BH 0.003) ? structure not eff [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: No elite creator produces a positive lineup-matched teammate-PPP lift at any lag.\n- observed_sample_and_power: Jokic lag-1 n=1880; Giannis n=1804; Doncic n=325\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF30\n- observed_verdict: null"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
